<!DOCTYPE html>
{#- Audit pack PDF. Layout only: every value comes from the manifest, every free-text
    value is autoescaped. Section letters match docs/design-notes/2026-09-23-insurer-audit-trail-plan.md §5. -#}
{% macro tier(t) %}<span class="tier tier-{{ t }}">{{ tiers[t][0] }}</span>{% endmacro %}
{% macro fix(f) %}{% if f %}{{ '%.5f'|format(f.lat) }}, {{ '%.5f'|format(f.lng) }}{% if f.accuracy_metres %} (±{{ f.accuracy_metres|round|int }} m){% endif %}{% else %}—{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Audit pack {{ issue.pack_label if issue else 'preview' }} — {{ m.trip.trip_reference }}</title>
<style>{{ css|safe }}</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="running running-pack">{{ issue.pack_label if issue else 'PREVIEW — not an issued pack' }}</div>
<div class="running running-trip">Trip {{ m.trip.trip_reference }}</div>
<div class="running running-issued">{% if issue %}Issued to {{ issue.recipient_name }}, {{ issue.recipient_organization }} for {{ purpose_label }} · {{ issue.pack_label }}{% else %}PREVIEW — not an issued pack{% endif %}</div>

{# ── §A Cover and verification summary ───────────────────────────────────── #}
<section id="cover">
  {% if not issue %}
  <div class="preview-banner">PREVIEW — this is not an issued pack. It is not sealed on Hedera and must not be relied on as evidence.</div>
  {% endif %}
  <h1>Trip Audit Trail</h1>
  <p class="muted">FreightProof evidence pack · generated {{ m.generated_at|sast }} · manifest v{{ m.manifest_version }}</p>

  <table class="kv">
    <tr><th>Trip reference</th><td>{{ m.trip.trip_reference }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Order number</th><td>{{ m.trip.order_number }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Operator</th><td>{{ m.trip.operator_name }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Client(s)</th><td>{{ m.trip.client_names|join(', ') or '—' }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Scope</th><td>{% if m.options.scope_consignment_id %}Single consignment: {{ m.consignments[0].parcel_perfect_reference if m.consignments else '—' }}{% else %}Whole trip{% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Trip status</th><td>{{ m.trip.status|humanise }}</td></tr>
    {% if issue %}
    <tr><th>Pack</th><td>{{ issue.pack_label }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Issued to</th><td>{{ issue.recipient_name }}, {{ issue.recipient_organization }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Purpose</th><td>{{ purpose_label }}{% if issue.external_reference %} · ref {{ issue.external_reference }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Issued by</th><td>{{ issue.issued_by_name }}, {{ issue.issued_at|sast }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Link valid until</th><td>{{ issue.expires_at|sast }}</td></tr>
    {% if issue.verify_url %}<tr><th>Verify online</th><td class="mono">{{ issue.verify_url }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  </table>

  <div class="summary-box">
    {% set phase_anchors = m.phases|selectattr('anchor_status', 'equalto', 'anchored')|list %}
    {% set owed = m.phases|selectattr('anchor_status', 'in', ['pending', 'failed'])|list %}
    {% set broken = m.anchored_records|rejectattr('payload_matches_hash')|list %}
    <strong>Integrity at generation:</strong>
    {{ m.anchored_records|length }} Hedera receipt(s) for this trip ·
    {{ phase_anchors|length }} anchored phase(s) ·
    {% if owed %}<span class="flag">{{ owed|length }} anchor(s) pending or failed</span>{% else %}no anchors owed{% endif %} ·
    {% if broken %}<span class="flag">{{ broken|length }} receipt payload(s) no longer match their hash</span>{% else %}every stored receipt payload matches its anchored hash{% endif %}.
    <p class="small muted">Checked against FreightProof's stored receipts when this pack was generated. Each hash can be
      re-checked independently against the public Hedera ledger using the steps in the integrity appendix.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>How to read this pack</h3>
  <table>
    {% for key, (label, meaning) in tiers.items() %}
    <tr><td style="width: 30mm">{{ tier(key) }}</td><td>{{ meaning }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  <p class="small muted">All times are South African Standard Time (SAST, UTC+2). Observations state what the record shows;
    they are not findings of fault.</p>
</section>

{# ── §B Observations ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
<section id="observations" class="page">
  <h2>Observations</h2>
  {% for o in m.observations %}
  <div class="obs obs-{{ o.level }}">{{ o.text }} <span class="code">[{{ o.code }}]</span></div>
  {% else %}
  <p class="muted">No observations.</p>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

{# ── §C Incident summary ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
{% if critical %}
<section id="incident">
  <h2>Incident summary</h2>
  {% set inc = m.incident %}
  <table class="kv">
    {% if inc %}
    <tr><th>First critical event</th><td>{{ inc.first_exception_type|humanise }}, {{ inc.first_raised_at|sast }} {{ tier('recorded') }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Where it was raised</th><td>{{ fix(inc.position) }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Last known position at or before it</th><td>{{ fix(inc.last_known_position) }}{% if inc.last_known_position %} · {{ inc.last_known_position.source|humanise }} · {{ inc.last_known_position.recorded_at|sast }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>First dispatcher review</th><td>{% if inc.first_reviewed_at %}{{ inc.first_reviewed_at|sast }} ({{ inc.minutes_to_first_review }} min after){% else %}<span class="flag">No review recorded</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% endif %}
    <tr><th>Vehicle(s)</th><td>{% for v in m.vehicles %}{{ v.registration }} ({{ v.role }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Driver</th><td>{{ m.driver.full_name }} · ID {{ m.driver.id_number }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Tracking devices</th><td>{% for v in m.vehicles %}{{ v.tracker_device_id }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Cargo</th><td>{% for c in m.consignments %}{{ c.parcel_perfect_reference }}{% if c.declared_value is not none %} (declared R {{ '{:,.2f}'.format(c.declared_value) }}){% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% else %}—{% endfor %}</td></tr>
  </table>
  <h3>Critical exceptions</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>#</th><th>Type</th><th>Raised</th><th>Description</th><th>Review</th></tr>
    {% for e in critical %}
    <tr><td>E{{ exception_numbers[e.exception_id] }}</td><td>{{ e.exception_type|humanise }}</td><td>{{ e.raised_at|sast }}</td>
      <td>{{ e.description }}</td><td>{{ e.review_status|humanise }}{% if e.review_note %}: {{ e.review_note }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  <h3>Police report and notifications {{ tier('declared') }}</h3>
  {% if m.declarations %}
  <table>
    <tr><th>Declared</th><th>SAPS</th><th>Reported</th><th>Notified</th><th>Claim ref / note</th></tr>
    {% for d in m.declarations %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ d.declared_at|sast }}<br><span class="small muted">by {{ d.declared_by_name or 'unknown' }}</span></td>
      <td>{{ d.saps_station or '—' }}{% if d.saps_cas_number %}<br>CAS {{ d.saps_cas_number }}{% endif %}{% if d.saps_officer %}<br>{{ d.saps_officer }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{{ d.reported_to_saps_at|sast }}</td>
      <td class="small">
        {% if d.client_notified_at %}Client {{ d.client_notified_at|sast }}<br>{% endif %}
        {% if d.insurer_notified_at %}Insurer {{ d.insurer_notified_at|sast }}<br>{% endif %}
        {% if d.tracking_company_notified_at %}Tracking co. {{ d.tracking_company_notified_at|sast }}{% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>{{ d.insurer_claim_reference or '' }}{% if d.note %}<br><span class="small">{{ d.note }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  <p class="small muted">Entered by the operator after the event; FreightProof did not capture these facts. Later
    declarations correct earlier ones and both are kept.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p class="small muted">No police report or notification times have been declared. A claim will need the SAPS station,
    case (CAS) number and the times the client, insurer and tracking company were told.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>
{% endif %}

{# ── §D Parties and trip plan ────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
<section id="plan" class="page">
  <h2>Trip plan and parties</h2>
  <table class="kv">
    <tr><th>Trip type</th><td>{{ m.trip.trip_type|humanise }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Created</th><td>{{ m.trip.created_at|sast }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Planned departure / arrival</th><td>{{ m.trip.planned_departure_at|sast }} / {{ m.trip.planned_arrival_at|sast }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Actual departure / arrival</th><td>{{ m.trip.actual_departure_at|sast }} / {{ m.trip.actual_arrival_at|sast }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Closed</th><td>{{ m.trip.closed_at|sast }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Tracking trip reference</th><td>{{ m.trip.pulsit_trip_reference_id or '—' }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Journey lock hash</th><td class="mono">{{ m.trip.journey_lock_hash or '—' }}</td></tr>
  </table>
  <h3>Stops</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>#</th><th>Precinct</th><th>Address</th><th>Slot</th><th>Geofence</th></tr>
    {% for s in m.stops %}
    <tr><td>{{ s.sequence }}</td><td>{{ s.precinct_name }}</td><td>{{ s.address or '—' }}</td><td>{{ s.slot_time|sast }}</td><td>{{ s.geofence_radius_metres }} m</td></tr>
    {% else %}
    <tr><td colspan="5" class="muted">No stops recorded.</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>

  {# ── §E Vehicles ── #}
  <h2>Vehicles</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Role</th><th>Registration</th><th>Make / model / year</th><th>VIN</th><th>Licence disc</th><th>Tracker</th></tr>
    {% for v in m.vehicles %}
    <tr><td>{{ v.role|humanise }}</td><td>{{ v.registration }}</td>
      <td>{{ v.make or '—' }} {{ v.model or '' }} {{ v.year or '' }}</td><td class="mono">{{ v.vin_number or '—' }}</td>
      <td>{{ v.licence_disc_expiry or 'not recorded' }}{% if v.licence_disc_valid_on_trip_date is true %} <span class="ok">valid on trip date</span>{% elif v.licence_disc_valid_on_trip_date is false %} <span class="flag">expired on trip date</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{{ v.tracker_device_id }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% if m.record_changes %}
  <h3>Driver and vehicle record changes during the trip</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>When</th><th>Record</th><th>Change</th><th>Fields</th><th>Tier</th></tr>
    {% for c in m.record_changes %}
    <tr><td>{{ c.changed_at|sast }}</td><td>{{ c.subject|humanise }}</td><td>{{ c.event_type|humanise }}</td><td>{{ c.changed_fields|join(', ') or '—' }}</td><td>{{ tier(c.tier) }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}

  {# ── §F Driver ── #}
  <h2>Driver</h2>
  <table class="kv">
    <tr><th>Name</th><td>{{ m.driver.full_name }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Identity number</th><td>{{ m.driver.id_number }}{% if m.driver.id_number_masked %} <span class="muted small">(masked)</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Licence number</th><td>{{ m.driver.license_number }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Licence expiry</th><td>{{ m.driver.license_expiry or 'not recorded' }}{% if m.driver.license_valid_on_trip_date is true %} <span class="ok">valid on trip date</span>{% elif m.driver.license_valid_on_trip_date is false %} <span class="flag">expired on trip date</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Professional driving permit (PrDP)</th><td class="muted">Not recorded by FreightProof</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Identity check for this trip</th><td>{{ m.driver.trip_idvs_status|humanise }}{% if m.driver.trip_idvs_checked_at %}, {{ m.driver.trip_idvs_checked_at|sast }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
  </table>
  {% if m.driver.substitutions %}
  <h3>Driver substitutions</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>When</th><th>From</th><th>To</th><th>Where</th><th>Planned</th><th>Tier</th></tr>
    {% for s in m.driver.substitutions %}
    <tr><td>{{ s.substitution_at|sast }}</td><td>{{ s.original_driver_name }}</td><td>{{ s.substituting_driver_name }}</td><td>{{ s.exchange_location }}</td><td>{{ 'Yes' if s.is_planned else 'No' }}</td><td>{{ tier(s.tier) }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}
</section>

{# ── §G Cargo ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
<section id="cargo" class="page">
  <h2>Cargo and consignments</h2>
  {% for c in m.consignments %}
  <h3>{{ c.parcel_perfect_reference }}{% if c.client_name %} · {{ c.client_name }}{% endif %}</h3>
  <table class="kv">
    <tr><th>Declared value</th><td>{% if c.declared_value is not none %}R {{ '{:,.2f}'.format(c.declared_value) }}{% else %}not declared{% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Parcels expected</th><td>{{ c.parcel_count_expected if c.parcel_count_expected is not none else '—' }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Units expected</th><td>{{ c.unit_count_expected if c.unit_count_expected is not none else '—' }}</td></tr>
  </table>
  {% if c.parcels %}
  <table>
    <tr><th>Barcode</th><th>Status</th><th>Scanned out</th><th>Scanned in</th></tr>
    {% for p in c.parcels %}
    <tr><td class="mono">{{ p.barcode }}</td><td>{{ p.status|humanise }}</td><td>{{ p.pp_scan_out_at|sast }}</td><td>{{ p.pp_scan_in_at|sast }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}
  {% else %}
  <p class="muted">No consignments are linked to this trip.</p>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

{# ── §H Custody chain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
<section id="custody" class="page">
  <h2>Custody chain</h2>
  <p class="small muted">One row per phase of the committed trip plan, in ledger order.</p>
  {% for p in m.phases %}
  <h3>P{{ p.sequence_number }} · {{ p.phase_type|humanise }}{% if p.precinct_name %} · {{ p.precinct_name }}{% endif %} {{ tier(p.tier) }}</h3>
  <table class="kv">
    <tr><th>Status</th><td>{{ p.status|humanise }}{% if p.overridden_by_dispatcher %} <span class="flag">dispatcher override</span>{% if p.override_note %}: {{ p.override_note }}{% endif %}{% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Completed</th><td>{{ p.completed_at|sast }}{% if p.slot_time %} · slot {{ p.slot_time|sast }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% if p.driver_phone or p.vehicle_tracker %}
    <tr><th>Driver phone</th><td>{{ fix(p.driver_phone) }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Vehicle tracker</th><td>{{ fix(p.vehicle_tracker) }}</td></tr>
    {% endif %}
    {% if p.location_assessment %}
    <tr><th>Location check</th><td>{{ p.location_assessment.proximity|humanise }}{% if p.location_assessment.separation_metres is not none %} · {{ p.location_assessment.separation_metres|round|int }} m apart{% endif %}{% if p.location_assessment.driver_in_precinct is not none %} · driver {{ 'inside' if p.location_assessment.driver_in_precinct else 'outside' }} precinct{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% endif %}
    {% if p.location_warning_acknowledged_at %}
    <tr><th>Location warning acknowledged</th><td>{{ p.location_warning_acknowledged_at|sast }}{% if p.location_warning_reason %}: {{ p.location_warning_reason }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% endif %}
    {% if p.seal_number %}<tr><th>Seal number</th><td>{{ p.seal_number }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% if p.parcel_count_origin is not none %}<tr><th>Parcels scanned out</th><td>{{ p.parcel_count_origin }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% if p.parcel_count_destination is not none %}<tr><th>Parcels scanned in</th><td>{{ p.parcel_count_destination }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% if p.driver_visual_count is not none %}<tr><th>Driver's count</th><td>{{ p.driver_visual_count }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% for e in p.evidence %}
    <tr><th>{{ e.role|humanise }}</th><td>{{ tier(e.tier) }} <span class="mono">sha256 {{ e.sha256 }}</span></td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
    {% for f in p.anchored_fields %}
    <tr><th>Anchored {{ f.name }}</th><td>{% if f.matches_anchor %}<span class="ok">matches Hedera</span>{% else %}<span class="flag">differs from Hedera</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
    <tr><th>Anchor</th><td>{{ p.anchor_status|humanise }}</td></tr>
  </table>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

{# ── §J In-transit record and §K Exceptions ──────────────────────────────── #}
<section id="transit" class="page">
  <h2>In-transit record</h2>
  <h3>Checkpoints</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>When</th><th>Type</th><th>Driver phone</th><th>Deviation</th><th>Note</th><th>Evidence</th></tr>
    {% for c in m.checkpoints %}
    <tr><td>{{ c.recorded_at|sast }}</td><td>{{ c.checkpoint_type|humanise }}</td><td>{{ fix(c.driver_phone) }}</td>
      <td>{{ 'Yes' if c.is_deviation else 'No' }}</td><td>{{ c.note or '—' }}</td><td>{{ c.evidence|length }} file(s)</td></tr>
    {% else %}
    <tr><td colspan="6" class="muted">No checkpoints recorded.</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>

  <h2>Exceptions and response log</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>#</th><th>Raised</th><th>Type / severity</th><th>Source</th><th>Description</th><th>Review</th></tr>
    {% for e in m.exceptions %}
    <tr><td>E{{ exception_numbers[e.exception_id] }}</td><td>{{ e.raised_at|sast }}</td>
      <td>{{ e.exception_type|humanise }} · {{ e.severity }}</td><td>{{ e.source|humanise }}</td><td>{{ e.description }}</td>
      <td>{{ e.review_status|humanise }}{% if e.reviewed_at %}, {{ e.reviewed_at|sast }}{% endif %}{% if e.reviewer_name %} by {{ e.reviewer_name }}{% endif %}{% if e.contact_method %} via {{ e.contact_method }}{% endif %}{% if e.review_outcome %} · {{ e.review_outcome|humanise }}{% endif %}{% if e.review_note %} · “{{ e.review_note }}”{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% else %}
    <tr><td colspan="6" class="muted">No exceptions recorded.</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  <p class="small muted">Exceptions are {{ tier('recorded') }} — FreightProof does not yet anchor exception records to Hedera.</p>
</section>

{# ── §L Location evidence ────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
<section id="location" class="page">
  <h2>Location evidence</h2>
  <div class="route">{{ route_svg|safe }}</div>
  <p class="small muted">Green circles: route precincts (geofence to scale). Blue line: driver-phone trail. Grey dashes:
    periods with no position. Purple squares: tracker fixes. Blue dots: checkpoints. Red diamonds: exceptions (E-numbers
    as in the exception log). No third-party map service was used to draw this.</p>
  {% set cov = m.location_coverage %}
  <table class="kv">
    <tr><th>Window assessed</th><td>{{ cov.window_start|sast }} → {{ cov.window_end|sast }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Fixes by source</th><td>{% for source, n in cov.fix_counts.items() %}{{ source|humanise }}: {{ n }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% else %}none{% endfor %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>First / last fix</th><td>{{ cov.first_fix_at|sast }} / {{ cov.last_fix_at|sast }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Coverage gaps</th><td>{{ cov.gaps|length }}</td></tr>
  </table>
  {% if cov.gaps %}
  <table>
    <tr><th>From</th><th>To</th><th>Length</th></tr>
    {% for g in cov.gaps %}<tr><td>{{ g.start|sast }}</td><td>{{ g.end|sast }}</td><td>{{ g.minutes }} min</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}
  {% if cov.stationary_periods %}
  <h3>Stationary periods outside route precincts</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>From</th><th>To</th><th>Length</th><th>Near</th></tr>
    {% for s in cov.stationary_periods %}<tr><td>{{ s.start|sast }}</td><td>{{ s.end|sast }}</td><td>{{ s.minutes }} min</td><td>{{ '%.4f'|format(s.lat) }}, {{ '%.4f'|format(s.lng) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}
  <p class="caveat">Phone positions are recorded only while the driver app is in use; the vehicle tracker is queried at
    handshakes and checkpoints. The absence of a position is not evidence that the vehicle was stationary, and a straight
    line between two positions is not evidence of the route driven.</p>
</section>

{# ── §M Integrity appendix ───────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
<section id="integrity" class="page">
  <h2>Integrity appendix</h2>
  <p>Each record below was reduced to a SHA-256 fingerprint and that fingerprint alone was published to the Hedera
    Consensus Service. No personal information is published. To check any record without relying on FreightProof:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Take the canonical payload exactly as printed (compact JSON, keys in alphabetical order).</li>
    <li>Compute its SHA-256 hash, encoded as UTF-8. It must equal the data hash shown.</li>
    <li>Open the Hedera mirror-node address shown and base64-decode the <span class="mono">message</span> field.
      It must equal the same data hash. The consensus timestamp shows when Hedera received it.</li>
  </ol>
  {% for r in anchored %}
  <h3>{{ r.receipt_type|humanise }} · {{ r.subject_type|humanise }}</h3>
  <table class="kv">
    <tr><th>Data hash (SHA-256)</th><td class="mono">{{ r.data_hash }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Stored payload matches hash</th><td>{% if r.payload_matches_hash %}<span class="ok">Yes</span>{% else %}<span class="flag">No — stored record altered after anchoring</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Hedera topic / sequence</th><td>{{ r.hedera_topic_id or '—' }} / {{ r.hedera_sequence_number if r.hedera_sequence_number is not none else '—' }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Transaction</th><td class="mono">{{ r.hedera_tx_id or '—' }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Consensus time</th><td>{{ r.hedera_consensus_at|sast }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Mirror node</th><td class="mono">{{ mirror_urls[r.receipt_id] or '—' }}</td></tr>
  </table>
  <pre class="payload">{{ r.canonical_payload }}</pre>
  {% else %}
  <p class="muted">No Hedera receipts are linked to this trip.</p>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

{# ── §N Methodology (ECT Act s15(3)) ─────────────────────────────────────── #}
<section id="methodology" class="page">
  <h2>How these records were produced</h2>
  <p class="small muted">Structured around the factors section 15(3) of the Electronic Communications and Transactions Act
    25 of 2002 directs a court to consider when weighing a data message.</p>
  <h3>How the records were generated</h3>
  <p>Custody events are captured by the driver in the FreightProof app at each handshake, with the phone's position and
    time. The vehicle's tracker (Pulsit) is queried independently at the same moment. Parcel scans come from Parcel
    Perfect. Driver identity checks come from an identity verification service. Each record carries the time the device
    captured it and the time the server received it.</p>
  <h3>How the records were stored</h3>
  <p>Records are held in a PostgreSQL database hosted in South Africa (af-south-1). Photos and documents are held in
    object storage, each with the SHA-256 hash of its bytes recorded at upload. The phase ledger is append-only: phases are
    completed, never rewritten.</p>
  <h3>How their integrity was maintained</h3>
  <p>At trip creation, departure and delivery confirmation, a canonical summary of the record — including the hashes of the
    seal, waybill and proof-of-delivery images — is hashed and published to the Hedera Consensus Service, a public ledger
    FreightProof cannot alter. A later change to any committed value no longer matches its published hash, and this pack
    reports every such mismatch. Records marked Recorded are not published and rely on FreightProof's own controls.</p>
  <h3>How originators were identified</h3>
  <p>Drivers and dispatchers sign in with individual accounts; every record stores the account that made it. Dispatcher
    overrides are recorded with the dispatcher and their stated reason.</p>
</section>

